  "caption": "Quinn walked to the letterbox and felt like they'd run a marathon. Aches everywhere, tired after a full night's sleep, and a foggy brain.\n\nFibromyalgia is linked to a pain system that has become extra sensitive, a bit like a smoke alarm that goes off when you make toast. That's why scans often look normal.\n\nThings that often help: start exercise smaller than you think and build slowly, pace yourself even on good days, protect your sleep routine, and learn how pain works. Progress is often gradual, with ups and downs.\n\nIf you've had widespread pain for months, start with your GP, who can rule out other causes and coordinate care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
